                <pb facs="0408" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2303: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-22T19:00:00+01:00">October 22, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:32 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>243. Drummond has handed me for communication to you the following message from
                    the Japanese delegation dated October 17, which has been circulated to the
                    members of the Council: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The troops from the Shingishu (Korea) garrison which had been sent to
                            Manchuria were all sent back to their garrison on the 16th <pb
                                facs="0409" n="299" xml:id="pg299"/> instant. I had the honor to
                            inform you in a previous letter that some of these troops were sent back
                            to Korea on September 28th.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
